# Custom CSS

Style the React client with plain CSS in project stylesheets. Do not add Tailwind, CSS-in-JS, or inline `style` objects.

- Put design tokens (`--text`, `--bg`, `--accent`, spacing, type) in `index.css` under `:root`.
- Put component styles in a colocated `.css` file and import it from the component (`import './App.css'`).
- Use class names and those tokens. Reuse existing variables before adding new ones.
- Support light and dark with the existing `prefers-color-scheme` block. Keep layouts usable at the `1024px` breakpoint.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — inline style */
<button style={{ background: '#aa3bff', padding: 8 }}>Save</button>

/* ✅ GOOD — class + token */
<button type="button" className="btn-primary">Save</button>
```

```css
.btn-primary {
  background: var(--accent);
  color: var(--bg);
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 8px 16px;
}
```
